---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Software', href: '/software/' }, { label: 'ClickFunnels Alternatives' }]} />
  <article>
    <header class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Alternatives guide</p><h1>Best ClickFunnels Alternatives in 2026: Compare the Stack You Actually Need</h1><p class="lede">The right replacement depends on what you use ClickFunnels for—not which competitor has the longest feature list.</p><p class="meta">Published September 10, 2026 · Pricing and features last verified September 10, 2026</p></div></header>
    <div class="narrow prose article-body">
      <AffiliateDisclosure hasRelationship={true} text="SelectVerdict has an affiliate relationship with Systeme.io. If you sign up through our Systeme.io link, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. That relationship does not determine our conclusions or inclusion criteria." />

      <p>If you are replacing ClickFunnels, start with a more useful question than “What is the best funnel builder?” Ask <strong>which parts of the ClickFunnels stack your business actually uses</strong>.</p>
      <p>ClickFunnels Launch currently costs $97 per month on monthly billing and includes unlimited funnels, 10,000 contacts, 50,000 emails per month, three courses, three communities, membership sites, one store, unlimited site and landing pages, and five custom domains. That makes ClickFunnels more than a page builder—and it makes many cheap-looking alternatives poor one-for-one comparisons.</p>
      <p>We compared six credible replacements by use case. We did <strong>not</strong> hands-on test these products for this article. Product facts and pricing below come from first-party vendor material checked September 10, 2026; the recommendations are SelectVerdict editorial judgments based on those verified facts.</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="ClickFunnels alternatives comparison"><table><thead><tr><th>Alternative</th><th>Best fit</th><th>Relevant starting point</th><th>Main trade-off</th></tr></thead><tbody>{alternatives.map((item) => <tr><th scope="row">{item.name}</th><td>{item.fit}</td><td>{item.price}</td><td>{item.tradeoff}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="source-note"><strong>Important:</strong> “Starting price” is not the same as “comparable ClickFunnels replacement.” The plan you need depends on contacts, email volume, courses, automation, checkout requirements and other functions you actually use.</p>

      <h2>What are you actually replacing in ClickFunnels?</h2>
      <p>A useful ClickFunnels comparison needs a baseline. Launch is currently $97/month, while Scale is $197/month and Optimize is $297/month on monthly billing. Launch includes 10,000 contacts and 50,000 monthly emails; Scale increases those to 75,000 contacts and 300,000 emails; Optimize to 150,000 contacts and 750,000 emails.</p>
      <p>Before choosing an alternative, write down which of these functions matter to you:</p>
      <ul><li>sales funnels and landing pages;</li><li>email sending and contact capacity;</li><li>marketing automation;</li><li>checkout, stores, upsells and order bumps;</li><li>courses, communities and membership delivery;</li><li>websites and custom domains;</li><li>workspaces, users and client accounts;</li><li>CRM, pipelines, booking, SMS or phone if those are part of your operation.</li></ul>
      <p>A platform can be cheaper and still cost more overall if you need three additional tools to recreate the workflow you had in ClickFunnels.</p>

      <h2>1. Systeme.io — best lower-cost all-in-one alternative</h2>
      <p>Systeme.io is the strongest value candidate when your goal is to keep funnels, email, automation, courses and selling tools under one roof without paying ClickFunnels-level subscription prices.</p>
      <p>Its current primary pricing page lists Free at $0, Startup at $17/month, Webinar at $47/month and Unlimited at $97/month. The Free plan supports up to 2,000 contacts; Startup raises that to 5,000; Webinar to 10,000; Unlimited removes the contact limit. Systeme.io also lists sales funnels, email marketing, website building, affiliate management, marketing automation, online courses, communities, booking, pipelines and webinars among its core tools.</p>
      <h3>Where it can replace ClickFunnels</h3>
      <p>For a solo business that needs funnels, email, automation, course delivery and checkout-related marketing features, the functional overlap is substantial. Systeme.io also states that its plans include unlimited email sending and no platform transaction fees.</p>
      <h3>Where the price comparison gets tricky</h3>
      <p>Do not compare ClickFunnels Launch's 10,000-contact allowance with Systeme.io Startup's 5,000 contacts and conclude that $17 replaces $97 for everyone. At 10,000 contacts, Systeme.io's relevant published tier is Webinar at $47/month. That is still lower than ClickFunnels Launch, but it is a fairer comparison.</p>
      <h3>Who should choose it?</h3>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> solopreneurs, creators and small online businesses that want an integrated funnel-and-marketing stack and care strongly about software cost.</p>
      <h3>Who should skip it?</h3>
      <p>If your reason for leaving ClickFunnels is that you need agency sub-accounts, a more specialized knowledge-business experience, or a particular funnel ecosystem, another alternative may fit better.</p>
      <p><a class="button" href={affiliateUrl} rel="sponsored nofollow">Try Systeme.io free</a></p>
      <p>For a deeper look, see our <a href="/reviews/systeme-io/">Systeme.io review</a>, <a href="/pricing/systeme-io/">Systeme.io pricing guide</a>, and <a href="/guides/systeme-io-free-plan/">Systeme.io Free plan analysis</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. GetResponse — best when email and automation drive the decision</h2>
      <p>GetResponse makes more sense than a generic funnel replacement when email marketing and automation are becoming the bottleneck.</p>
      <p>At the 1,000-contact tier, current monthly pricing starts at $19 for Starter, $59 for Marketer and $69 for Creator. Starter includes unlimited monthly email sends, landing pages and one custom automation workflow—but <strong>does not include sales funnels</strong>. Marketer adds unlimited automation workflows, advanced segmentation, abandoned-cart recovery, sales funnels, promo codes and revenue reports. Creator adds webinars, a website builder, course creation and up to 500 students.</p>
      <h3>Why Marketer is the more relevant ClickFunnels comparison</h3>
      <p>The $19 Starter headline price is not a fair funnel-stack comparison because GetResponse's own documentation says sales funnels are unavailable on Starter. For a business specifically replacing funnels plus email automation, Marketer at $59/month is the more relevant entry point at 1,000 contacts.</p>
      <h3>What you gain</h3>
      <p>You get an email-centered platform with segmentation and automation at the center of its architecture rather than as one component of a funnel suite.</p>
      <h3>What you lose</h3>
      <p>GetResponse prices scale with list size, and not every ClickFunnels function maps neatly to the same plan. A course business may need Creator; a pure email-and-funnel business may not.</p>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> businesses where email, segmentation and automation matter more than staying inside a funnel-first ecosystem.</p>

      <h2>3. HighLevel — best for agencies and multi-client operations</h2>
      <p>HighLevel is not simply another funnel builder. Its pricing and product architecture are built around businesses that may manage multiple client accounts.</p>
      <p>Starter is currently $97/month and includes three sub-accounts, unlimited contacts and unlimited users. Unlimited is $297/month and removes the sub-account limit. Agency Pro is $497/month and adds SaaS Mode and automated sub-account creation. HighLevel's core feature list includes website and funnel building, CRM and pipelines, email and SMS marketing, calling, workflows, forms and surveys, booking calendars, payments, courses and communities.</p>
      <h3>Why switch from ClickFunnels?</h3>
      <p>The strongest reason is not cheaper funnels. It is the need for CRM, pipelines, client sub-accounts, multi-channel communication and agency infrastructure in one environment.</p>
      <h3>What you lose</h3>
      <p>Simplicity. HighLevel also marks several communications and AI capabilities as usage-based, so subscription price alone is not total cost of ownership.</p>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> agencies, consultants and client-service businesses that genuinely need sub-account architecture.</p>
      <p><strong>Skip it if:</strong> you are a solo creator looking mainly for a simpler or cheaper funnel stack.</p>

      <h2>4. Kartra — best for a broader integrated marketing stack</h2>
      <p>Kartra belongs in this comparison because it competes at the integrated-stack level: pages and funnels, products and checkout, email, automation, memberships/courses and related marketing operations.</p>
      <p>Its Essentials plan is positioned as the entry tier, but one economic detail matters more than the sticker price: Kartra's July 2026 help documentation confirms a <strong>5% transaction fee</strong> on each sale or rebill for products hosted in Kartra on Essentials. Other Kartra plans are not subject to that Essentials fee.</p>
      <h3>Why that fee changes the comparison</h3>
      <p>At $5,000 in monthly net hosted-product sales, a 5% platform transaction fee equals $250 before considering the subscription itself or payment-processing costs. That means an entry plan can become more expensive than a higher-priced subscription as sales grow.</p>
      <h3>Who should choose it?</h3>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> businesses that want an integrated marketing platform and can justify its plan economics with the capabilities they actually use.</p>
      <p><strong>Skip it if:</strong> your primary goal is simply reducing software cost. Evaluate total cost, not only the advertised subscription.</p>

      <h2>5. Kajabi — best for course and knowledge businesses</h2>
      <p>Kajabi is a credible ClickFunnels alternative when the product itself is knowledge: courses, memberships, coaching or a creator-led business. It is not the budget option.</p>
      <p>Current monthly pricing is $179 for Basic, $249 for Growth and $499 for Pro. Basic includes five products, 2,500 contacts, one website, one community and two admin users. Growth increases that to 50 products and 25,000 contacts, while Pro lists unlimited products and 100,000 contacts.</p>
      <h3>Why switch?</h3>
      <p>If courses and the customer learning environment are the center of the business rather than an accessory to a funnel, Kajabi's product orientation becomes more relevant.</p>
      <h3>What you lose</h3>
      <p>The obvious trade-off is cost. Even Kajabi Basic costs substantially more than ClickFunnels Launch on monthly billing, so the switch needs to be justified by business-model fit—not by a generic feature count.</p>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> established knowledge businesses that want the platform organized around products, audience and community.</p>
      <p><strong>Skip it if:</strong> the main reason you are leaving ClickFunnels is price.</p>

      <h2>6. Simvoly — best when you want a website and funnels together</h2>
      <p>Simvoly's differentiator is the way it combines websites, funnels, ecommerce, CRM, communities and marketing tools. Its current pricing material shows plans with website and funnel capacity, store products, subscriptions, upsells, bump offers and CRM, while email and automation capacity is tied to subscriber allowances and add-ons.</p>
      <h3>Why switch?</h3>
      <p>If you want your main website and sales funnels managed as one connected property rather than treating the funnel as a separate marketing layer, Simvoly deserves consideration.</p>
      <h3>What you lose</h3>
      <p>Its plan structure is not directly comparable with ClickFunnels. Funnel count, website count, communities, marketing subscribers and email volume vary by configuration, so a single low headline price can be misleading.</p>
      <p><strong>Best fit:</strong> businesses that value an integrated website + funnel + ecommerce architecture.</p>

      <h2>ClickFunnels alternatives compared by business scenario</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="ClickFunnels replacement scenarios"><table><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Start with</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Solo business, funnels + email + courses, cost-sensitive</th><td>Systeme.io</td><td>Broad overlap with materially lower published tiers</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Email and automation are the bottleneck</th><td>GetResponse Marketer</td><td>Sales funnels plus unlimited automation workflows at the relevant tier</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Agency managing multiple clients</th><td>HighLevel</td><td>Sub-accounts, CRM, pipelines and agency architecture</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Integrated marketing stack with heavier operations</th><td>Kartra</td><td>Broad marketing-stack orientation; compare transaction economics carefully</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Courses and knowledge products are the core business</th><td>Kajabi</td><td>Product/community-focused architecture</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Website and funnels should live together</th><td>Simvoly</td><td>Website + funnel + ecommerce structure</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>

      <h2>How much can you actually save?</h2>
      <p>ClickFunnels Launch is $97/month on monthly billing. A few comparisons illustrate why equivalent use cases matter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Systeme.io Startup at $17/month</strong> is $80 below ClickFunnels Launch, but Startup supports 5,000 contacts rather than Launch's 10,000. At the 10,000-contact level, Systeme.io Webinar at $47 is the more relevant published tier.</li>
        <li><strong>GetResponse Marketer at $59/month</strong> is $38 below ClickFunnels Launch at the 1,000-contact tier, but GetResponse pricing rises as the list grows.</li>
        <li><strong>HighLevel Starter at $97/month</strong> has the same sticker subscription price as ClickFunnels Launch, but it is solving a different problem: client sub-accounts, CRM and agency operations.</li>
        <li><strong>Kajabi Basic at $179/month</strong> costs $82 more than ClickFunnels Launch, so it is a business-model switch, not a savings play.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These are subscription comparisons, not promises of total savings. Payment processing, transaction fees, communications usage, add-ons and extra software can change the real cost.</p>

      <h2>Is there a good free alternative to ClickFunnels?</h2>
      <p>Systeme.io is the clearest full-stack free candidate in this comparison. Its current Free plan is $0, supports up to 2,000 contacts and includes three sales funnels, one course and the platform's core tool set. It does not require a credit card and the plan does not expire according to Systeme.io's current pricing material.</p>
      <p>That does not mean it is a free equivalent of ClickFunnels Launch. ClickFunnels Launch includes far larger allowances in several areas. The free plan is most useful for validating a small funnel business before paying for capacity.</p>

      <h2>Who should stay with ClickFunnels?</h2>
      <p>Switching software has a cost even when the new subscription is cheaper. You may need to rebuild pages, reconnect domains, move contacts, recreate automations, migrate courses, reconnect payments and verify tracking.</p>
      <p>Staying with ClickFunnels is rational when your current funnels work, its limits fit your operation, your team already knows the platform, and the expected benefit of moving is smaller than the migration cost and operational risk.</p>
      <p>A useful decision rule is:</p>
      <p><strong>Switch only when the value of the missing capability or recurring savings is greater than the migration cost, added complexity and disruption.</strong></p>

      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>Choose based on the bottleneck, not the brand:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cost + broad all-in-one functionality:</strong> start with Systeme.io.</li>
        <li><strong>Email + automation depth:</strong> compare GetResponse Marketer.</li>
        <li><strong>Agency/client infrastructure:</strong> start with HighLevel.</li>
        <li><strong>Broader integrated marketing operations:</strong> evaluate Kartra's relevant paid tier and transaction economics.</li>
        <li><strong>Courses/knowledge business:</strong> compare Kajabi against the actual course and community workflow you need.</li>
        <li><strong>Website + funnels in one architecture:</strong> evaluate Simvoly's relevant plan rather than its lowest advertised configuration.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If none of those problems describes your situation, changing platforms may be unnecessary.</p>

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <h3>What is the best ClickFunnels alternative?</h3>
      <p>There is no universal winner. Systeme.io is the strongest lower-cost all-in-one candidate in this comparison; GetResponse is more compelling when email and automation are central; HighLevel fits agencies; Kajabi fits knowledge businesses; Simvoly fits website-plus-funnel use cases; and Kartra is worth evaluating for a broader integrated marketing stack.</p>
      <h3>Is Systeme.io a real ClickFunnels alternative?</h3>
      <p>Yes. The platforms overlap across funnels, email, automation, courses and selling tools. But plan limits differ, so compare the tier that matches your contact count and workflow rather than comparing $17 with $97 in isolation.</p>
      <h3>Is GetResponse cheaper than ClickFunnels?</h3>
      <p>At the current 1,000-contact tier, GetResponse Marketer is $59/month versus ClickFunnels Launch at $97/month. GetResponse pricing scales with list size, so that difference is not fixed for every business.</p>
      <h3>Can I replace ClickFunnels for free?</h3>
      <p>For a small operation, Systeme.io's Free plan can cover funnels, email and related core functions within its limits. It is not a capacity-equivalent replacement for ClickFunnels Launch.</p>
      <h3>Should I move away from ClickFunnels just to save money?</h3>
      <p>Not automatically. Calculate subscription savings against migration work, missing features, add-ons and the risk of disrupting a working funnel. A cheaper tool is only cheaper if it supports the workflow you need.</p>

      <h2>Verdict</h2>
      <p>For most cost-sensitive solo businesses looking for a broad ClickFunnels replacement, <strong>Systeme.io is the first alternative we would evaluate</strong> because its verified pricing and feature scope overlap with a large part of the ClickFunnels stack. That is a value judgment, not a claim that the two platforms are identical.</p>
      <p>If your reason for switching is more specific, choose accordingly: GetResponse for email and automation, HighLevel for agency operations, Kajabi for a knowledge business, Simvoly for website-plus-funnel architecture, or Kartra when you need a broader integrated marketing stack and its economics make sense.</p>
      <p><a class="button" href={affiliateUrl} rel="sponsored nofollow">Compare Systeme.io starting with the Free plan</a></p>

      <SourceBlock sources={sources} />
      <p class="source-note"><strong>Methodology:</strong> We used first-party vendor pricing, help and product materials for changeable facts. We did not hands-on test these six alternatives for this article. Comparative recommendations are editorial judgments derived from the cited product scope, limits and pricing. Prices and features can change after our verification date.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
